SUMMARY:Monarch Tagging Demo
DESCRIPTION:Join the Monarch Monitoring Project team to learn about the Monarch butterflies that migrate through Cape May\, as well as the ongoing research and outreach our staff is doing to help protect the species. After the talk\, watch as small tags are affixed to Monarchs to track their migration to Mexico. And best of all\, you’ll learn how you can contribute to Monarch conservation! NO preregistration required. Family-friendly \nMeeting Location: Meets at the East Shelter located next to the Hawkwatch platform at the Cape May Point State Park \nCost: FREE – contributions to the Monarch Monitoring Project are welcome.  \nInterested in becoming a member? Please click on the following link to learn more or join: Become a Member today! \n\n 
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/monarch-tagging-demo-11/2026-09-13/
LOCATION:Cape May Point State Park – East Shelter\, NJ\, United States
CATEGORIES:Cape May Bird Observatory,Cape May Bird Observatory's Northwood Center,Family Program,Monarchs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/Monarch-Tagging-Demo_Eventbright_2160x1080.jpg
GEO:38.933008140108;-74.95813540732
END:VEVENT
