SUMMARY:Half Day Fridays at Sandy Hook
DESCRIPTION:Early fall birding at the hook: we may encounter anything from shorebirds and terns to flycatchers\, sparrows\, and warblers. A wide variety of habitats ensure good bird diversity at one of the state’s best spots. Be prepared for 3-4 hours of walking over flat and sandy surfaces. Led by Scott Barnes and associate naturalists. \nLocation: Meet at Parking Lot B\, about halfway down the lot by the bathrooms \nPRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nCOST: $25 Members\, $30 Non-members \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/half-day-fridays-at-sandy-hook-54/
LOCATION:Sandy Hook – Lot B\, Hartshorne Drive\, Sandy Hook\, NJ\, 07732\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
